Wait, that was my original which derefed *ai.Run when nil... no wait, original was `duration := *ai.Run; if critical { duration = *ai.Critical }` — for a critical-only action, ai.Run is nil → deref nil at `*ai.Run`. The panic at line 184 in the first run was that. Now I inverted it and run-only actions panic. Correct version:

```go
var duration int64
if ai.Run != nil {
    duration = *ai.Run
} else {
    duration = *ai.Critical
}
```

